+# Core/2 staged-test R3 source and frozen data packet
+
+This candidate adds moriarty-tests/2 to public `mori test`, consuming the actual
+local Core/2 load/start/resume APIs and comparing complete reports. Its normal
+tests invoke the public binary path. All builds, CLI runs, tests and runtime
+comparisons remain UNRUN. Native authority remains zero.
+
+The prior complete candidate was blocked by the final Opus source review. Both
+original scenarios carried duty liabilities absent from the programs' source
+registry, so actual R7 would reject their awaiting starts. Prior data approvals
+and literal-data agreement did not establish valid positive trajectories. The
+original candidate/worktree, inputs, expectations, reviews and partial-oracle
+history are preserved. Their positive-data approvals are historical and invalid.
+
+R3 appends an unused matching-duty declaration action to each program. Neither
+action is invoked by the target delivery/fee path. A separately blinded author
+then derived fresh whole-program and two-action plan preimages, six complete
+reports and normal source-admission premises including full R7. Root verified
+the24 bound files,8 inputs,4 preimage hashes, exact25-file oracle copy,21-file
+blocked-input archive and all current report/preimage byte identities. These
+are literal-data/source checks, not observations of the interpreter.
+
+P-TRACE-PROJ/draft remains a source-derived attachment/presence convention.
+Other parser, serialization, digest, plan, meter and admission premises remain
+disclosed. C1–C6 and historical N1–N6 retain only their stated scope. All fourteen
+draft gaps remain open, including the prior contradicting R7 observation. No
+semantic correctness, financial/native validity, proof, printed-format result,
+Rust/Quint/Lean/circuit correspondence or U0–U7/M1–M17/MC/SP/G exit is claimed.
+
+Immutable captures preserve exact original bytes, including obsolete partial,
+review-pending and approval labels. They describe their original inputs. The
+final REVIEW-BINDING records only actual fresh dispositions for the R3 source,
+frozen normal data and proposed draft publication. Source publication does not
+admit Cargo, SDK execution, terminal retries, native proving or ledger work.
+Frozen assembly scripts with original paths are provenance, not portable public
+commands, and were not executed by this source integration.
