+# Staged-test fixture provenance
+
+The current root six reports and four whole-program/stage-plan preimages are
+exact copies of the separately authored
+[R3 normal-data freeze](independent-oracle-r3/INDEPENDENT-FREEZE.json), SHA-256
+`ad44178b801dc51bfa6e254a2d9b48c18a4f7ea99e7b919be75730dc761cc34d`.
+The complete freeze and its 24 bound members are preserved byte for byte.
+Author: `/root/mori_test_stages_oracle`, GPT-6.1 Sol high. The
+[derivation](independent-oracle-r3/DERIVATION.md),
+[eight input pins](independent-oracle-r3/input-sha256.json) and
+[normal accounting](independent-oracle-r3/normal-accounting-and-work.json)
+identify the exact source/data premises and complete candidate content.
+
+This is reversible source/data integration, not a program-output comparison.
+Builds, tests, public CLI/evaluator execution and actual-output comparisons are
+**UNRUN**; comparison admission is **NOT_GRANTED** and native authority is **0**.
+Source/data/publication review dispositions belong to the
+[final audit binding](../../docs/audits/2026-10-16/core-staged-tests-r3/REVIEW-BINDING.json),
+which Root must supply before publication. No approval is assumed here. Immutable
+capture-time review-pending fields in the frozen records remain historical;
+consult that binding for later dispositions. No runtime/printed-byte-format,
+financial/native, proof or parent-roadmap acceptance follows from this data.
+
+## R7 premise and complete program identity
+
+Final Opus review `mori-test-stages-final-opus-r1` blocked the original positive
+expectations: both scenarios carried a duty, but neither original source
+registered its identity. Existing awaiting-start admission and resume boundary
+checks require exact liability identities from source Liability statements
+across all program actions. The
+[R3 source-admission inventory](independent-oracle-r3/ADMISSION-PREMISES.md)
+records that premise and the other original admission conditions. Consistency
+with those source conditions is neither a correctness proof nor an observed
+admission pass.
+
+Each revised program appends an unused `declare` action after its target action:
+TwoDeliveries registers duty/UNIT/alice/bob; QuotedFee registers
+duty/UNIT/payer/treasury. These amount-0 statements are not executed by the
+selected deliver/charge trajectories. Incoming duty5/duty3 remain in the
+unchanged scenarios; declaration presence implies no creation or discharge.
+The full preimages include both actions and all eight expression nodes.
+No parser, evaluator, compiler or admission function generated the expectations.
+
+The [canonical digest record](independent-oracle-r3/canonical-digests.json)
+binds the independently authored full preimages:
+
+| Program | Whole-program SHA-256 | Stage-plan SHA-256 |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| TwoDeliveries | `582b7923087e42b46c318576ad4bb786904b7ac0691a6c4580ed2deb187afe44` | `d9f7cba42cd4ce1dc1f70544a3592b8a0aba984c8f5cd779c3716d26ca1ac575` |
+| QuotedFee | `3eae05c146cda49dfb7364c3ff106018d356fefae95c1239eab2ad2c0a74339e` | `a1638d25988da7569769048911324a6cc8ea160c4a85366386221df768a32a6b` |
+
+## Independence and retained limits
+
+R3 was freshly derived from the two revised sources, six unchanged scenario/
+event inputs and disclosed source/normative material. It did not read old author
+or oracle expectations/preimages to construct the new reports. The literal
+assembly script is preserved as source and was not run by this integration.
+The manifest names the six root report files; each is byte-identical to its R3
+freeze member. That is static data identity, not agreement with actual output.
+
+P-TRACE-PROJ/draft remains an unadopted, source-observed attachment/presence
+premise only. Parser allocation, JSON/type/envelope shapes, canonical encoding,
